README.md:7:CLI tools built for humans produce verbose, formatted output with ANSI colors, alignment padding, and all fields included. When AI agents consume this output, they pay 1.5-5x more tokens than necessary. MCP servers fix the format but add ~2,200 tokens of session overhead (tool definitions) and don't support batching.
README.md:21:### Why Not MCP?
README.md:23:- **Session overhead:** ~2,200 tokens of tool definitions loaded per session
README.md:24:- **No batching:** each query is a separate tool call (~80 tok framing each)
README.md:25:- **Break-even:** ~293 queries per session (unrealistic for typical agent work)
README.md:26:- **Identical output:** MCP and DSL return the same JSON when backed by the same field selection engine
README.md:28:See [references/comparison-example.md](references/comparison-example.md) for a detailed measurement on a real 346-element board.
